# Watchdog fixture: run from the repository root (wdg.sh does this).
#
# The reset macro is required, not cosmetic: Renode logs "No action for reset"
# and keeps the CPU parked unless a reset action reloads the image. With it, an
# IWDG expiry restarts Reset_Handler while .noinit survives, which is what lets
# boot 2 report the latency measured in boot 1.
#
# Virtual time is bounded at 300 ms: ~32 ms runaway + reset + ~100 ms healthy
# control loop, with margin. Nothing here depends on wall-clock time.
using sysbus
mach create "coact-wdg"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/boards/stm32f4_discovery.repl
sysbus.usart2 CreateFileBackend @test/renode/build/wdg.log true

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF @test/renode/build/coact_wdg.elf
"""
runMacro $reset

emulation RunFor "00:00:00.300"
quit
